===persian===

این صدای سم اسبان است
با رپ رپه طبل ها ...
تو را در برکه های هذیانی تبهایم
بر اسب میبینم
اسب می ماند.
سم می کوبد...
سر می ساید
تو خاموشی...
و من لبهایم را
به بلندترین فریاد گشوده ام.
نسیم از دریا به جنگل در گذار است
تو میشنوی که میگویم
دوستت دارم...
نگاهت آفتابی میشود.
سایه اسب بر ساحل مینشیند
اسب میرمد
رعد در بال
باد در پاها...
هنوز لبانم به بلندترین فریاد گشوده است
فریاد در جنگل میپیچد
بمان...
جنگ تمام خواهد شد....
پرندگان مانده اند... بمان... دوستت دارم...
تو... می روی...
و... من لحظه دیشب در سر
لحظه امشب در دل
به پناهگاه بر می گردم...

زمستان ۱۳۶۶

===machine===

This is the sound of horses' hoofs
With the rap of the drums...
I will bathe you in delirious pools.
I see on a horse
The horse stays.
The hoof knocks...
head rubs
You are silent...
And I my lips
I have opened the loudest cry.
The breeze is passing from the sea to the forest.
You hear me say.
I love you...
Your gaze becomes sunny.
The shadow of a horse sits on the shore.
The horse dies
Thunder in the wings
Wind in the legs...
My lips are still open to the loudest scream.
A scream echoes through the forest
stay...
The war will end.
The birds have stayed... Stay... I love you...
you... go...
And... I was thinking about it last night.
Tonight's moment in the heart
I'm going back to the shelter...

Winter 1366

===lantern===

This is the sound of horses' hooves,
with the rat-a-tat of drums...
In the delirious pools of my fever
I see you on horseback.
The horse halts.
A hoof pounds...
it rubs its head.
You are silent...
and I have opened my lips
in the loudest cry.
The breeze is crossing from the sea to the forest.
You hear me saying
I love you...
and your gaze turns sunny.
The horse's shadow settles on the shore.
The horse bolts —
thunder in its wings,
wind in its legs...
Still my lips are parted in the loudest cry,
the cry goes winding through the forest:
Stay...
the war will end...
the birds have stayed... stay... I love you...
You... are leaving...
and I — last night's moment in my head,
tonight's in my heart —
turn back to the shelter...

Winter 1366

